p Hi #{USERNAME},
if MFA_ENROLLED
  p Multi-factor authentication was turned on for your account. Signing in now asks for a code from your second factor after your password.
else if MFA_REPLACED
  p The multi-factor authentication of your account was replaced by a new one. The previous second factor and its recovery codes no longer work.
else if MFA_DEACTIVATED
  p Multi-factor authentication was turned off for your account. Signing in now asks for your password only.
else if MFA_RECOVERED
  p Multi-factor authentication was removed from your account with a recovery code. Signing in now asks for your password only.
else if MFA_DEACTIVATED_BY_ADMIN
  p Multi-factor authentication was turned off for your account by an administrator of your platform. Signing in now asks for your password only.
else
  p The multi-factor authentication settings of your account changed.
p If you made this change, you can ignore this email. If you did not, change your password right away, turn multi-factor authentication back on, and contact the support of your platform.
